From: luckfox-linux <build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] rknpu: do not dereference a NULL vdd regulator

rknpu_probe() gets the NPU supply with devm_regulator_get_optional(),
and when the board has no rknpu-supply it deliberately keeps going with
a NULL pointer:

	rknpu_dev->vdd = devm_regulator_get_optional(dev, "rknpu");
	if (IS_ERR(rknpu_dev->vdd)) {
		if (PTR_ERR(rknpu_dev->vdd) != -ENODEV) {
			...
			return ret;
		}
		rknpu_dev->vdd = NULL;
	}

That is the normal state on the RV1106: the NPU shares VDD_LOGIC with
the rest of the SoC, there is no separate rail to describe, so the
driver runs without one. The power paths agree - both the runtime-PM
enable and disable sites test rknpu_dev->vdd before touching it - and
the devfreq readers are only reachable once rockchip_init_opp_table()
has succeeded, which it cannot do without a supply.

Two readers never got the memo and hand the NULL straight to
regulator_get_voltage(), which dereferences it:

  - rknpu_volt_show(), behind /sys/kernel/debug/rknpu/volt and
    /proc/rknpu/volt. Reading that file oopses the kernel.
  - the RKNPU_GET_VOLT ioctl on /dev/rknpu, which is reachable by any
    process that can open the render node.

Test for the supply in both. The debug node returns -ENODEV, which
seq_file passes back to read(2) as an error rather than printing a
made-up voltage; the ioctl keeps its ABI and reports 0, since callers
treat it as an informational reading and an unexpected error there
would fail whole inference sessions over a diagnostic.

Signed-off-by: luckfox-linux <build@localhost>
---
 drivers/rknpu/rknpu_debugger.c | 3 +++
 drivers/rknpu/rknpu_drv.c      | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_debugger.c b/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_debugger.c
index b3caca8..cf06a0e 100644
--- a/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_debugger.c
+++ b/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_debugger.c
@@ -252,6 +252,9 @@ static int rknpu_volt_show(struct seq_file *m, void *data)
 		container_of(debugger, struct rknpu_device, debugger);
 	unsigned long current_volt = 0;
 
+	if (!rknpu_dev->vdd)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	current_volt = regulator_get_voltage(rknpu_dev->vdd);
 
 	seq_printf(m, "%lu\n", current_volt);
diff --git a/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_drv.c b/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_drv.c
index a0af79b..a2907fa 100644
--- a/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_drv.c
@@ -436,7 +436,9 @@ static int rknpu_action(struct rknpu_device *rknpu_dev,
 		break;
 	case RKNPU_GET_VOLT:
 #ifndef FPGA_PLATFORM
-		args->value = regulator_get_voltage(rknpu_dev->vdd);
+		args->value = rknpu_dev->vdd ?
+				      regulator_get_voltage(rknpu_dev->vdd) :
+				      0;
 #endif
 		ret = 0;
 		break;
